*(
    title: Effects of the Environment on Organisms
    description: The pressures a habitat applies, and how they change which organisms are found in it.
    tags: selection pressure, abiotic, biotic, distribution, module 3, biology, stub
    lesson
)

@include(src: ../preface.part.chalk)

scene{
    An environment does not affect every individual in a species equally, and that unevenness is the whole mechanism. Where conditions differ across a range, the organisms found at each point differ too.

    Written out here: abiotic and biotic selection pressures, their effect on the distribution and abundance of species, and what happens to a population when the environment changes faster than the population can — including the conditions under which extinction rather than adaptation is the outcome.
}
